menu "SimpleOTA"

config SIMPLEOTA_TASK_STACK_SIZE
    int "OTA task stack size (bytes)"
    default 12288
    help
        The managed task performs TLS handshakes (esp_http_client with the
        certificate bundle) and cJSON parsing on its own stack. 8192 usually
        works; the 12288 default leaves headroom on all targets.

config SIMPLEOTA_TASK_PRIORITY
    int "OTA task priority"
    range 1 20
    default 5
    help
        Priority of the managed OTA task. Keep it below the Wi-Fi and lwIP
        tasks (the default 5 is) so networking is never starved.

config SIMPLEOTA_HTTP_TIMEOUT_MS
    int "HTTP timeout (ms)"
    default 15000
    help
        Socket timeout for the check, status, and download requests. During
        a download this doubles as the stall detector: a read that makes no
        progress for this long fails the update with reason
        "download_stalled".

config SIMPLEOTA_HTTP_TX_BUFFER
    int "HTTP client TX buffer (bytes)"
    default 2048
    help
        Must fit the entire request line and headers. Pre-signed download
        URLs are routinely 500-1500+ characters, which overflows the
        esp_http_client default of 512 bytes.

config SIMPLEOTA_DOWNLOAD_CHUNK
    int "Download/flash chunk size (bytes)"
    default 4096
    help
        Heap-allocated buffer used to stream the firmware image from the
        HTTP client into the OTA partition while hashing and verifying.

config SIMPLEOTA_DISABLE_TRIAL_WATCHDOG
    bool "Leave the chip watchdog alone during a trial"
    default n
    depends on BOOTLOADER_APP_ROLLBACK_ENABLE
    help
        On a trial boot the component starts the chip's RTC or LP watchdog
        for the confirm timeout plus a margin, so a hang that stops the
        confirm timer still resets the chip and the bootloader switches
        back. Enable this to skip that watchdog. The confirm timer still
        runs, and a crash still switches back through the bootloader.

endmenu
